1
00:00:03,681 --> 00:00:04,708
Hi everyone!

2
00:00:04,834 --> 00:00:07,948
I'm back today

3
00:00:08,721 --> 00:00:12,748
with a tutorial on the "drag seat".

4
00:00:13,541 --> 00:00:18,114
For the "drag seat", you first need
to be comfortable riding "seat out".

5
00:00:19,027 --> 00:00:23,907
Before letting go of the saddle,
here are two exercises for you.

6
00:00:25,974 --> 00:00:30,187
The first exercise is riding
with the saddle held far out in front.

7
00:00:31,361 --> 00:00:35,594
This exercise gets you used to riding
without putting any weight

8
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:40,793
on the saddle,
and smooths out your "seat out" riding.

9
00:00:44,727 --> 00:00:48,618
The second exercise is riding "seat out"

10
00:00:48,689 --> 00:00:50,013
without your hands on the saddle.

11
00:00:52,081 --> 00:00:54,395
To stop the saddle
from falling to the ground,

12
00:00:54,687 --> 00:00:56,773
squeeze your knees together
in front of the frame.

13
00:01:00,467 --> 00:01:04,974
This exercise gets you
into the right "drag seat" position

14
00:01:05,514 --> 00:01:06,927
and makes you bend your knees properly.

15
00:01:08,721 --> 00:01:11,228
Once you're comfortable
with these two exercises,

16
00:01:11,352 --> 00:01:13,254
you can start letting go of the saddle.

17
00:01:13,994 --> 00:01:15,947
There are two techniques
for letting go of the saddle.

18
00:01:16,454 --> 00:01:21,221
Either you hold the saddle
and guide it out as far as possible

19
00:01:21,327 --> 00:01:23,020
before letting it drop to the ground.

20
00:01:24,267 --> 00:01:29,340
Or you put your hand on the frame
and guide it all the way down.

21
00:01:32,741 --> 00:01:35,443
What's important, and not easy at first,

22
00:01:35,694 --> 00:01:37,677
is that when you let go of the saddle,

23
00:01:37,701 --> 00:01:40,828
the cranks must be parallel to the ground.

24
00:01:41,194 --> 00:01:42,880
So, both pedals at the same height.

25
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,515
When you start letting go
of the saddle,

26
00:01:47,767 --> 00:01:50,388
it helps to combine
the two previous exercises.

27
00:01:51,074 --> 00:01:54,533
First, ride "seat out"
without holding the saddle

28
00:01:54,557 --> 00:01:56,074
to get into the right position.

29
00:01:56,447 --> 00:02:02,027
Then grab the saddle, push it forward
as far as you can, and let go.

30
00:02:04,434 --> 00:02:06,588
Once you've let go of the saddle,

31
00:02:06,654 --> 00:02:10,634
try to keep a good rhythm
and move as smoothly as you can.

32
00:02:11,301 --> 00:02:14,014
Keep your knees bent
and your back straight.

33
00:02:14,607 --> 00:02:18,240
Try to spread your weight
evenly over both pedals.

34
00:02:18,306 --> 00:02:30,361
[Music]

35
00:02:30,427 --> 00:02:33,056
Now on to the hardest part:

36
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:35,640
picking the saddle back up
after the "drag seat".

37
00:02:36,681 --> 00:02:41,735
To do this, bend your knees,
grab the frame just above the fork,

38
00:02:41,859 --> 00:02:45,648
then slide your hand up to the saddle.

39
00:02:46,147 --> 00:02:48,668
Always keep your back straight
and your knees bent.

40
00:02:48,894 --> 00:02:51,453
Don't lean forward, or you'll fall.

41
00:02:51,519 --> 00:02:59,428
[Music]

42
00:02:59,494 --> 00:03:00,785
Here too, it's important

43
00:03:00,851 --> 00:03:05,213
to bring the saddle up
while the pedals are at the same height,

44
00:03:05,313 --> 00:03:06,875
with the cranks parallel to the ground.

45
00:03:07,607 --> 00:03:10,301
If you bring the saddle up
with one pedal down,

46
00:03:10,394 --> 00:03:13,567
the saddle will swing to the side
and throw you off balance.

47
00:03:15,008 --> 00:03:18,388
If you have any questions
or need some advice,

48
00:03:18,647 --> 00:03:23,360
feel free to leave a comment
and I'll be happy to answer.

